\id WIS 71-WIS-obbe.sfm Orthodox Bible in British English (OBBE)
\usfm 3.0
\ide UTF-8
\rem Editor: Fr Deacon David Hoskin
\h Wisdom
\toc1 Wisdom of Solomon
\toc2 Wisdom of Solomon
\toc3 Wisdom
\mt1 Wisdom of Solomon
\c 3
\v 1 The souls of the righteous are in the hand of God and no torment shall touch them.
\v 2 In the eyes of the foolish they seemed to die. Their departure seemed lamentable:
\v 3 they were going from us to utter destruction. But they are at peace.
\v 4 For though in the eyes of mortals they were punished, yet their hope is full of immortality.
\v 5 And having been chastised for a while, they shall be richly rewarded; for God has proved them, and found them worthy for himself.
\v 6 Like gold in the furnace he tested them, and accepted them as a whole burnt offering.
\v 7 And at the time of their visitation they will shine, and dance to and fro like sparks among the stubble.
\v 8 They will judge the nations and have dominion over peoples, and their Lord will reign for ever.
\v 9 Those who put their trust in him will know the truth, and those who are faithful will remain with him in love. For grace and mercy are upon his holy ones, for he watches over his chosen.
\c 4
\v 7 Though the righteous may be the first to die, yet they shall be at rest. 
\v 8 For an honourable age is not established by length of time, nor measured by the number of years, 
\v 9 yet people think that wisdom is grey hair, and that an unspotted life means old age. 
\v 10 He pleased God and was loved by him, so that while living among sinners he was translated. 
\v 11 Yes, he was taken quickly so that evil should not change his understanding, nor deceit beguile his soul. 
\v 12 For being bewitched by wickedness obscures what is honest; and restless greed undermines the simple mind. 
\v 13 He was made perfect in a short time, fulfilling long years. 
\v 14 Because his soul pleased the Lord, he hurried to take him from among the wicked.
\v 15 The people saw this but did not understand, nor store in their minds that his grace and mercy are with his chosen ones, and that he watches over those who are holy.
\c 5
\v 15 The righteous live for ever and their reward is in the Lord, for they are in the care of the Most High.
\v 16 They shall therefore receive a glorious crown, and a beautiful diadem from the hand of the Lord; for with his right hand he will cover them, and with his arm he will protect them.
\v 17 He will take his zeal as his complete armour, and arm creation to repel his enemies.
\v 18 He will put on righteousness as a breastplate, and just judgement for a helmet;
\v 19 and he will take holiness as an invincible shield.
\v 20 His great wrath he will sharpen for a sword, and the world will fight with him against the foolish.
\v 21 Then the well-aimed thunderbolts will be loosed, and from the clouds, as from a well-drawn bow, they will fly to the mark.
\v 22 And hailstones, full of wrath, will be flung like stone shot, and the waters of the sea will rage against them, and the floods will cruelly overwhelm them.
\v 23 A mighty wind will rise against them, and like a tempest it will blow them away. Lawlessness will lay waste the whole earth, and iniquity will overthrow the thrones of rulers. 
\c 6
\v 1 Therefore listen, you kings, and understand; learn, you judges of the ends of the earth.
\v 2 Give ear, you who rule a multitude and exult over many nations,
\v 3 for your power is given to you by the Lord, and sovereignty is from the Most High.
